.TH VBLK 4
.SH NAME
vblk \- the disk server (port "disk")
.SH SYNOPSIS
Port
.BR disk .
A boot module, started by
.BR init (8)
with device rights; restarted if it ends (the requests to it are simply
sent again).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vblk
serves SIEOS's disk in 4 KiB blocks to its only client, the file server
.BR fs (4).
The disk is, in this order:
a virtio block device (QEMU's virtio-blk, PCI on x86-64, MMIO on arm64);
on arm64 an SD card (the Raspberry Pis);
the first NVMe namespace with a SieFS partition;
the first USB disk with a SieFS partition (from
.BR usb (4)).
A drive without a SieFS partition is never used: a PC's own drives hold its
other systems.
.PP
With the boot option
.BI root= GUID
(the UEFI loader's
.BR boot.cfg (5)),
the disk is the SieFS partition with that unique GUID, on whichever drive it
is.
Partitions: a GUID partition table (the SieFS partition by its type), or an
MBR (type 0x5E); a disk without either is SieFS whole if a superblock says so.
.PP
No copies of its own: a client's data arrives by IPC straight into the buffer
the device reads, and read data is copied out from where the device wrote it.
One request at a time, up to 128 KiB each.
.SH MESSAGES
.TP
.B DISK_INFO
\-> the number of 4 KiB blocks; reply w[1] = the SD controller's physical
address when the disk is an SD card (0: not).
.TP
.B DISK_READ
w[1] = first block, w[2] = count; the data comes in rbuf. \-> 0.
.TP
.B DISK_WRITE
w[1] = first block, w[2] = count; the data in sbuf. \-> 0.
.TP
.B DISK_FLUSH
make every write so far durable. \-> 0.
.TP
.BR DISK_RAW_INFO ", " DISK_RAW_READ ", " DISK_RAW_WRITE ", " DISK_RAW_FLUSH
(root: the installer) the PC's NVMe drives whole, in their own sectors:
w[1] = the drive, w[2] = first sector, w[3] = count; DISK_RAW_INFO fills a
disk_raw_t (model, serial, sector size, sectors; \-ENOENT: no more drives).
\-EBUSY while SIEOS itself runs from an NVMe drive.
.PP
A message moves at most DISK_MAX (128 KiB).
The USB server's
.BR usbdisk N
ports speak the same protocol.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fs (4),
.BR usb (4),
.BR siefs (5),
.BR install (8)
